~ maze_system
Guide: Yeahhh, that tracks. The U.S. insurance system is basically a maze designed by a committee of wizards who didn't coordinate their spells.
Guide: One second you're just trying to find a therapist, and then suddenly you're staring at words like "deductible," "copay," and "allowed amount," wondering if you accidentally enrolled in a finance course.
Guide: And when your mental health is already struggling? Trying to decode all this feels like playing a boss fight with half your stats missing.
Guide: Let me ask you something though — When someone says "in-network" or "out-of-network"... what happens inside your brain?
- My brain shuts off instantly.
